description:
In repos/goal-host-vessel/src/index.ts, replace exactly one line so a landed commit is no longer treated as proof the goal was achieved.

Background. The helper landedShaForGoalHash currently returns a sha as soon as git finds a commit carrying the goal hash. That proves work LANDED; it does not prove the work did what the goal asked. Measured 2026-09-03: dispatch b64c330f landed commit 023f9b1 for route-edit-c10beb80, the goal was "make a duplicated sentence appear exactly once", the sentence still appeared twice afterwards, and this helper graded the dispatch reached:true. That is a false positive.

The compose report is the right corroborating evidence and is now trustworthy. It was previously unusable because a failed retry overwrote it after a successful landing, but development-vessel commit ce10c8b fixed that: a FAVORABLE report carrying a landed sha is preserved and the failed retry is written to a sibling file. Confirmed in production 2026-09-04 on route-edit-39ce0192, whose FAVORABLE report survived an UNFAVORABLE retry five minutes later.

Find this exact single line, which appears once in the file:

    return /^[0-9a-f]{40}$/.test(out) ? out : null;

Replace that one line with:

    if (!/^[0-9a-f]{40}$/.test(out)) return null;
    // A COMMIT IS NOT AN ACHIEVEMENT. The sha proves work landed; it does not prove the
    // work did what the goal asked (measured: 023f9b1 for route-edit-c10beb80 landed and
    // the goal was NOT met, and this helper graded it reached:true). Demand the same
    // corroboration the crash-recovery reconciler further down this file demands: a
    // FAVORABLE compose report carrying a cutover new_git_sha. That report is trustworthy
    // again since ce10c8b stopped a failed retry from overwriting a favorable one.
    // Every doubt below returns null, so this can only ever WITHHOLD a reach, never invent
    // one — which is the property the doc comment above claims and did not previously hold.
    try {
      const reportFile = Bun.file(`/workspace/proposals/route-edit-${h}-compose-report.json`);
      if (!(await reportFile.exists())) return null;
      const report = JSON.parse(await reportFile.text()) as Record<string, unknown>;
      if (report.verdict !== "FAVORABLE") return null;
      const cutovers = Array.isArray(report.cutovers) ? (report.cutovers as Array<Record<string, unknown>>) : [];
      const landed = cutovers.some((c) => {
        const res = (c?.result ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>;
        return typeof res.new_git_sha === "string" && res.new_git_sha.length > 0;
      });
      if (!landed) return null;
    } catch {
      return null;
    }
    return out;

This is a ONE-OP change. Replace only that single return statement. Do not add any import — the replacement uses only Bun.file and JSON.parse, both already available in this file, which already reads /workspace/proposals paths in five other places. Do not edit the doc comment above the function, do not touch any other function, and do not modify any other file.

